# Coding standards

## Repeatable results

- Before implementing: write the step plan, file list, and success criteria — show them to the user before saving code
- Surgical changes — edit only what the task requires
- Do not "improve" neighboring code, comments, or formatting
- Match the existing style even if you would do it differently
- If the task is ambiguous — ask before coding
- Do not add npm/cargo dependencies; use the existing stack

## Simplicity

- Minimum code that solves the problem, nothing speculative
- No abstractions for one-off use
- No features nobody asked for
- If 200 lines can be 50 — rewrite

## No leftover mess

The agent cleans **its own** diff before calling the task done:

- Remove unused imports, variables, parameters, types, functions, and files that you added or that your change made dead
- Do not leave commented-out code, debug `console.log` / `println!`, throwaway `TODO`, or `#[allow(dead_code)]` as a sweep-under
- Do not export "just in case". Do not create helpers, types, or constants unused in the same diff
- After edits, lint touched files and fix warnings you introduced
- Do not touch pre-existing dead code that your change did not cause — unless the user asks

## Domain determinism

- Every terrain-generation change MUST keep seed → world determinism
- Test with seed `6` (Ellipse) as the baseline
- After a shape/biome/noise change, check that `seed % 6` still maps to the same profile

## Language

- Code comments: English
- Agent files (`AGENTS.md`, `.cursor/rules`, `.cursor/skills`): English
- Project docs (README, `docs/`): Polish
